    "title": "The rapid rise of cheating in Olympiad competitions reduces their prestige - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Terence Wang ,\n1 days ago Achieving success in Olympiads such as the USA Math Olympiad (USAMO) and the USA Coding Olympiad (USACO) is seen as a big accomplishment, often recognized by colleges and universities and set as a lifelong goal for thousands of teens. However, many of these accomplishments are now being undermined by cheating, which has become much more prevalent with the rise of AI and online answers. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
